Specifically, src/borgclj/buzhash_table.clj contains the 256-entry buzhash
table taken verbatim from BorgBackup's content-defined chunker. The table is
not incidental: borg-clj must produce the same chunk boundaries as borg, or
the archives it writes would not deduplicate against archives written by borg
itself.

The repository format, the msgpack framing of its objects, the remote
protocol spoken over ssh and the layout of the archive metadata are likewise
modelled on BorgBackup so that the two interoperate. Those parts are an
independent implementation written against borg's on-disk and on-the-wire
behaviour rather than a translation of its source.

borg-clj is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a product of the BorgBackup
project.
